        ],
        "text": "Petitioners were represented by Paul\u202fW.\u202fHughes, Esq., and the respondent was represented by Frederick\u202fLiu, Assistant to the Solicitor General."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioners",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "9e0320f4515ed0c5f442e97fce632f2a39ec3d94c0ebf69acea49820d93f0041",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-9e0320f4515e-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 5,
              "start": 5
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Petitioners argue that Section\u202f(2)(D) provides for review of questions of law decided by the Board of Immigration Appeals and that courts may review whether the Board identified the proper legal standard."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Liu",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "9e0320f4515ed0c5f442e97fce632f2a39ec3d94c0ebf69acea49820d93f0041",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-9e0320f4515e-0002-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 47,
              "start": 47
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. Liu, the government contends that Congress intended to give criminal aliens no judicial review."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Liu",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "9e0320f4515ed0c5f442e97fce632f2a39ec3d94c0ebf69acea49820d93f0041",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-9e0320f4515e-0002-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 48,
              "start": 48
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. Liu, the government further states that since 1996 the goal has been to expedite the removal of criminal aliens."
      }
